This file gathers and re-exports the results of Scott's section 2 on LAMBDA: continuity and the union and bottom laws for minimal extension; continuity of successor and predecessor; the basic element coded by 1; continuity of the conditional in each argument and the conditional laws for bottom, top, numerals, the empty set, mixed and positive indices, and the case split; left continuity of application and continuity of diagonal application, the identity, constants, and graphs of continuous components; commutation of environment update and continuity of interpretation in a variable; Theorem 2.1; the beta, xi, and alpha clauses and Theorem 2.2; currying and Theorem 2.3 in the unary, binary, ternary, and finite cases; Theorem 2.4 with its complete and closed forms, combinatory interpretation, and the correctness of abstraction and erasure; the omega combinator, diagonal unions, and the first recursion theorem, Theorem 2.5; the Y combinator, its application, unfolding, combinatory character, and the interpretation of its term; the numbered laws (2.1), (2.5) through (2.7), (2.9) through (2.18), (2.22) through (2.25), (2.27), and (2.28), including the sequence, recursion, intersection, and dollar-step forms; the mu law of Table 1; the beta laws for successor, predecessor, K, S, and the conditional, the expression of union by the conditional, and the identity S K K; the failure of eta and the xi-star law; the search for a least element; and the continuity, application, iteration, and fixed-point laws for the dollar step, primitive recursion, and their term forms.
